   "translations": [
    {
     "id": 97131,
     "resource_id": 20,
     "text": "So they set out, until when they came to the people of a town, they asked its people for food, but they refused to offer them hospitality. And they found therein a wall about to collapse, so he [i.e., al-Khiḍr] restored it. [Moses] said, \"If you wished, you could have taken for it a payment.\""
    }
   ]
